# Lore any realm can talk about: Darkness Falls and Legion's court, the tunnels under the three frontiers,
# the dragons compared, con colours, drop superstitions, the world still finding itself, swimming to the
# edge of the world, old maps, hidden rooms, GM nights and player legends, and promised things that never
# came. Classic and Shrouded Isles (up to 1.65) only. New writing for this project.
#
# Truth rules for this file: documented lore is said plainly; rumours, superstitions and inventions are
# framed as hearsay, belief, memory or argument. No bot claims to have killed Legion, Behemoth, Govannon
# or a dragon. Realm * only: no place names except Darkness Falls and the battlegrounds, and every line
# that compares the realms treats all three the same.

@kind ambient
@topic lore
@realm *
@about place

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Darkness Falls: Legion's court
@who NoLifer
@levels 30-50
legion keeps a court down there like a king. princes, high lords, dukes, earls, marquises, and every demon knows its rank
[three demon princes|three princes] [sit|stand] under legion, and [each one|every one] of them would wipe a careless group
prince abdin, prince asmoien, prince ba'alorien. say them three times and see who shows up
the dukes in df are where most raids [find out|learn] [how big the gap is|they were not ready]
i like to think grand chancellor adremal keeps legion's books. even demons need clerks
field marshal nebir drills legion's army, or so the old raiders say
gatekeeper dommel has not left that door since df opened, or so the story goes
[heard|i hear] the chthonic knights stop [most raids|whole raids] long before anyone sees legion
legion takes less damage than you would think, or so every raid leader says after the wipe
[word is|heard] legion can send people straight into behemoth's room, and [that is the end of your evening|nobody walks back out]
even legion has a chamberlain. somebody has to sweep the floors
mutilator xagalith has the most honest title in the whole of darkness falls
i have walked past the dukes so often i know them by name. [alloc, aypol, bimure|sallis, satori, zepor], old neighbours
the earls down there have names no bard could rhyme. zh'alzhak, glassalab, ipostian, i ask you
back when df first opened nobody knew what a duke was. we learned on our corpses
i remember the first time someone typed legion in faction. the whole realm went quiet for a minute
nobody i know has seen every room in darkness falls, and i know some very stubborn people

@who NoLifer,Explorer
@levels 30-50
behemoth [cant be killed|does not die]. [every guild that tried says the same|i have heard it from three guilds], nothing sticks to him
people say behemoth takes no damage at all. others say nobody has brought enough people yet
level ninety nine and parked in a room doing nothing. behemoth is either guarding something or bored
[i think|my guess is] behemoth is not a monster at all, he is a lock, and nobody has found the key

@who *
@levels 20-50
the imps in df rob the bigger demons and trade the loot for seals. little thieves with a proper trade
a bright seal is worth more than a dull one, [even the imps know that|that is the whole df economy]
whoever holds the most keeps opens df. count the keeps before you pack
[df|darkness falls] changes hands [more often than the weather|like the weather]. check before you ride out
darkness falls was a story long before it was a dungeon. a few old timers swear they fought there in another life
[i like to think|i think] the demons were down there ages before any of us found the portal
[some say|people say] df feeds on the realm war. the more keeps change hands, the deeper it runs
they say the demons crawled up out of the deep once the three realms went to war with each other
ask an imp and i bet the realm war is the best thing that ever happened to them

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the Summoner's Hall and Govannon
@who NoLifer,Explorer
@levels 35-50
grand summoner govannon starts the fight as an elf and finishes it as a demon. nobody knows which one is the real him
[the old raiders say|word is], leave govannon's shield node alone or [every hit does one damage|your swords might as well be sticks]
heard a govannon fight runs forty minutes. bring food, and a spare healer
aidon the archwizard waits in the summoner's hall like he owns it, and nobody can say whose side he is on
three summoners, an archwizard and sidhe guards, all in one hall. someone planned that
the summoners in that hall keep calling something. nobody i know has asked them what
[heard|people say] the deepest rooms of df lead to the summoner's hall, where all three realms come together
i heard the summoner's hall was a sidhe place before legion's lot moved in

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the tunnels and the third power
@who Explorer,NoLifer
@levels 20-50
someone dug tunnels under all three frontiers and filled them with undead. [who is the third power|nobody ever says who]
the tunnels under the frontier were not dug by albs, mids or hibs. something else wants all three of us
[i think|my guess is] the tunnels and the summoner's hall are one plan. someone is calling the dead from all three realms at once
the dead in the tunnels serve a power nobody has named, and i do not think it is legion
while three realms fight over keeps, something is digging under all of us. funny how that goes
every realm found tunnels under its own frontier, and every realm swears it found them first
i followed a tunnel [until my torch ran low|as far as i dared], and it went further than any map said
i bet whoever dug the tunnels also drew the old maps. explains a lot

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the dragons compared
@who *
@levels 30-50
wolf, stone or glimmer, which dragon is oldest? every realm says its own
three realms, three dragons. a wolf, a stone and a glimmer, and every realm thinks theirs is the worst
golestandt, gjalpinulva, cuuldurach. one for each realm, and every bard has a song for theirs
[heard|people say] the dragons have never met. probably for the best, one of them would eat the other two
[i think|my guess is] the three dragons are kin, scattered [across the realms|to the three realms] long before any of us
an old raid leader told me never nuke a dragon early. let the tanks get it settled first
half of every raid comes for the respec stones, not the loot. fifty stones a dragon
[those|the] luminescent stones are the real hoard. the dragon is only the lock on the chest
dragons drop nothing but coin, or so the bitter ones say
[heard|i hear] bring over a hundred people to a dragon and it [goes berserk|loses its temper]. so leave the cousins home
i heard dragons talk to your corpse after they kill you. not sure i want to know what they say
some swear killing the big giants nearby takes a dragon's fire away. i swear they are drunk
a dragon is just a big lizard until it breathes on you. then it is a religion
dragon lairs [smell of old coin and bad decisions|reek of burnt hair and regret]
i asked a town guard about the dragon once. he told me to go home. very helpful
heard the three dragons dream about each other. a bard probably made that up, but i like it
legend says the first group to find a dragon was a lost explorer who took a wrong turn
ask [an alb|a mid|a hib] and their dragon is the oldest. ask anyone else and you get two more answers
i remember when nobody knew the dragons existed, until some fool wandered into a lair

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the frontier giants
@who Explorer,Daredevil
@levels 25-50
each frontier has an old giant that belongs to no realm: a green knight, a glacier giant and evern. walk around them
[heard|people say] the glacier giant throws people [half a zone|clear across the frontier], and folks used to bet on where they land
the green knight leaves you alone unless you start it. wise people keep riding
[heard|i hear] evern gets healed by fairies landing on [its|the] stones. fairies first, always

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- con colours
@who *
@levels 10-50
the con colours lie. i once saw [an orange|a yellow] gut a full group
never trust a con on anything with a name. the colour is a mood, not a level
half the named mobs show one colour and hit like another, and the bestiaries cant agree either
purple is purple. there is no colour for run now, and there should be
my theory is the con colours were set by someone who never pulled anything
blue cons have killed more of us than reds ever did. nobody respects a blue

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- drop superstitions
@who Crafter
never say the item's name in chat while you camp it. my old guild swore the mob hears
[my old guild|an old guildmate] swore drops are better if you /bow to the corpse before looting
some people think rare drops come right after a server reset. i think they just remember the good nights
i knew a crafter who would not loot with a full bag. said the rare could tell
first kill after you log in [always|never] drops the good stuff, depending who you ask
[old wisdom says|they say] drops improve the moment the whole camp stops talking about them
i keep a lucky ring in my pack for rare drops. it has not worked once. still wont sell it
dragon scales would make amazing armor, if only someone would let crafters near one
@who *
the stealth folk claim drops come better if you open from behind. of course they would
a healer friend never loots first. says the luck follows whoever was humble
if the named pops right as you go afk, [that is not luck, that is a curse|that is a curse], and everyone knows it
never camp one spot too long after dark. old superstition says the camp starts noticing

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the world finding itself
@who Explorer
the islands just turned up one autumn, [as if they had always been there|like they were always there]. bet there are more
every realm has a story about a pass that came out of the mist one day where no pass had been
there is always one more dungeon nobody has found yet. always
every year someone finds a new cave and [everyone acts surprised|acts surprised]. i stopped being surprised
[i bet|i think] the world goes further than any map they sell
[the old maps|my old map] [show|shows] roads that are not there anymore. either the mapmaker was drunk or the world moved
i still keep a first map with half the coast missing. it was more honest
the old maps had whole stretches marked unknown. best part of the map
half the fun early on was not knowing what was over the next hill
nobody charted the far corners properly. i swear there are caves nobody mentions
i keep a journal of spots i stumbled into that show up on no map
every realm has a tale about a lost place that the older maps almost show
some sages say the gods are still drawing the world, one island at a time
the bards claim the land was half the size at the start, and it grows a little each year
heard there is a vendor out in the wilds who sells maps of places that do not exist yet
when i see a ledge nobody talks about, in i go. usually it is just a bear
found a ruined wall once that nobody could name. still wondering whose it was
every ridge looks climbable right up until you slide back down
i could swear the fog out past the coast moves when nobody is looking
a sage told me the fog at the edge of the world is the gods' unfinished work. makes sense to me
real explorers never ask directions. we get lost on purpose
best kind of evening: no group, no plans, just riding toward a coastline nobody bothered with
i still wonder who carved the old markers out in the wilds. half of them point at nothing
[an old|a] [hunter|ranger|scout] swore the wild beasts remember the old roads the maps forgot
heard of a guy who logged out on a rock at the edge of the world and logged in somewhere nobody recognised

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the edge of the world
@who Explorer
every map ends in water, but the water does not end. swim far enough and you hit the wall the gods put there
i once swam out until the water went dark. then nothing, just a wall you cannot see
[heard|people say] if you swim far enough out the [fog gets thicker|water turns grey], and then there is just a wall
a friend swam to the edge of the world and came back saying the sky just stops
[i think|my theory is] the wall at the edge is there to keep something out, not to keep us in
the edge of the world is real, i swam into it. like cold glass under the sea
nobody can say what is beyond the wall. i asked a sage once, he told me to go level
a swim to the edge takes forever. bring patience, the view is worth it
heard there is an island out past the last map's edge that you can see but never reach
@who Daredevil
[i dare|dare] anyone to swim to the edge [in full plate|in their armor] and back
one day i will swim to the edge with no speed buff, just to say i did

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- hidden rooms
@who Explorer
every dungeon has a room behind the room. never found one myself, but i check every wall
[heard|people say] there is a wall in one of the old dungeons that only opens [when nobody is watching|for a group of one class]
i once walked along every wall of a dungeon hunting a secret door. all i found was [a rat|a spider]
some corners in the old dungeons look built for something that never moved in. gives me chills
an old bard told me every crypt has one sealed room nobody opens. i half believe it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- GM nights and player legends
@who Socialite
i remember a gm night where the whole town turned out for a poetry contest. weirdest evening in years
heard a gm once held a funeral for a player right out in the frontier. i like to think nobody attacked
every realm has a legend about one player who held a bridge alone. i believe all of them
heard of a [bard|minstrel|skald] who dragged a whole camp across a zone and lived. [probably a lie|i want it to be true]
you hear about healers who never died once all the way to fifty. nobody i know has met one
old raid leaders turn into legends faster than the dragons do
some names in the old herald rankings feel more like myth than people now
i swear i once saw a gm stroll through a town in a funny hat. nobody believes me
[rumour is|they say] a gm sometimes rides the roads [in disguise|disguised as a nobody]. be polite to strangers, just in case
word is the imps know every rumour in all three realms. i should ask them
the best part of a good legend is that nobody can prove anything
[heard|people say] the old gods still walk the roads now and then. i wave at every stranger
nothing beats a good ghost story at the bind stone

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- promised things
@who NoLifer
the devs promised more relics years ago. still six on the pedestals
six relics, two per realm. there were supposed to be more. i keep wondering where they are
[i think|my theory is] the missing relics are buried out there, waiting for someone to stumble on them
some say the other relics were never made. i like the version where they sit in a chest somewhere
every patch someone swears new relics are coming. every patch, nothing
we were promised more relics back at the start. we got islands instead
every realm guards two relics and swears its pair is the oldest
albs have their lost city, mids have their lost hall, hibs have their door under the hill. everyone has a place they cant find

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- general lore musings
@who *
every realm swears its legends are the oldest. i think all three are right
legends never die, they just grow another verse each time a bard sings them
half of lore is people who wiped explaining why
the oldest lesson in the game: if it has a name, it has a grudge
the battlegrounds have their own ghosts too. every one has a hill where someone stood against ten
heard a renegade chieftain in the battlegrounds remembers every face that ever beat him
nobody ever explains why the dead keep getting up in all three realms. we just kill them twice

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- is it worth it, and dares
@who Leveler
@levels 30-50
dragon raids are three hours of standing around for a stone. i will level instead
df is decent xp while your realm holds it, and useless the rest of the week
legion lore is fun, but lore never gave anyone a bubble
@who Daredevil
@levels 30-50
i dare someone to run up to behemoth just to wave. once
one day i will tag a duke in df alone, just to see what happens
someday i will stand where legion can see me and not run. someday

# ================================================================ debates
@kind debate
@realm *

@topic lore_behemoth
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_behemoth_killable
@role B type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=Explorer levels=30-50
A: {q} is behemoth really unkillable, or is that a story the raid leaders tell | {q} anyone else think behemoth can die and nobody has managed it yet
?D: wait, who is behemoth? i keep seeing the name in faction | whos behemoth? sounds like a boat
B: the biggest thing in darkness falls. level ninety nine, a room to himself, and nothing you swing at him sticks | a demon in df, level ninety nine, not a typo. he has his own room and every hit on him does nothing
D: ninety nine? i thought fifty was the top | how is anything ninety nine, i thought fifty was as high as it goes
E: fifty is our cap. legion's court goes way past it. dukes in the mid seventies, the princes near eighty, legion in the eighties | we stop at fifty, the demons dont. duke alloc and his lot are about seventy five, the three princes nearer eighty
C: and behemoth sits sixteen levels over legion himself. so who is really in charge down there | sixteen levels over his own master. if i were legion i would sleep with one eye open
B: thats the odd part. legion keeps a proper court. three princes, four high lords, the dukes, earls and marquises, a chancellor | every demon there has a rank. prince abdin, high lord baln, duke aypol, earl vone. a chancellor and a field marshal even
B: behemoth has no title at all. no prince, no lord. just behemoth | and behemoth? no rank, no seat at the court. just the name
E: a thing with no rank is not a servant. its something they keep. a pet, or a prisoner | no title means he is not part of the court. legion keeps him, he doesnt serve
C: or the bouncer | or the thing legion feeds the people he doesnt like to
B: half right. the raid leaders say legion can port people straight into behemoth's room in the middle of the fight | the old raiders swear legion sends people to behemoth's room mid fight, and nobody walks back
D: so he's like a bin for players legion is done with | so legion throws you away and behemoth is the bin
C: a bin that hits harder than your whole health bar | a very angry bin
E: in the old books behemoth is the great beast of the land, and only the one who made him can bring a sword near him | the old scripture tale says behemoth is the first of the beasts, and only his maker can come at him with a blade
E: so maybe none of us can kill him because none of us made him | which would mean the game is telling us straight: this one is not for you
B: or nothing sticks and that is that. three guilds told me the same: you swing, you cast, you dot, the numbers dont move | three raid leaders, three realms, same story. melee, nukes, dots, nothing comes off him. thats not lore, thats a wall
C: walls have doors. maybe its a phase thing like govannon's node. break something else first and he opens up | a mob that cant die is a puzzle. find the right thing to break first
B: people looked. the rooms near him are full of chthonic knights and earls, and killing them does nothing to him | the knights and earls round his room get farmed for seals all week. nobody ever saw him flinch
~ 15
D: has anyone tried with a whole realm at once? | what if every level fifty in the realm went in together
E: people say bring more and he just takes more, like rain on a lake | i heard a hundred went in once. the bards stopped counting the corpses
C: i still say nobody brought enough people | everything dies if you hit it long enough
B: everything with hit points. i am not sure he has any | everything that can bleed. i am not convinced he can
?D: maybe he is why the demons stay down there. maybe they're scared of him | maybe legion isnt his master, maybe legion is his jailer
C: next time df is ours im walking up to his doorway just to wave | someday i stand in his doorway and wave. just once
E: take a scout. someone should write down what that room looks like before you die | wave from the door and type out what you see. nobody has described that room properly
B: i'll hold your bind point | dont expect a rez from me

@topic lore_tunnels
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_third_power
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role D type=Socialite
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: who actually dug the tunnels under the frontiers? nobody ever answers that | {q} whose work are those tunnels under all three frontiers
B: the dead did the digging. but the dead dont make plans, somebody gave them the plans | undead did the shovelling. undead dont draw plans though
?E: wait, tunnels? under the frontier? | there are tunnels under the frontier? since when
C: since the summer after darkness falls opened. one under each frontier, all three found the same season, all full of undead | they turned up the summer after df came. three of them, one per frontier, all crawling with the dead
C: and the heralds said it plain: they serve a new power that wants all three realms. never said whose | the herald's word was a power that means to rule all three realms. a name? never one
B: so who wants all three of us at once? not one of us three. nobody else is fighting on every front | which power hates every realm the same? not albs, not mids, not hibs
D: legion. obviously. he hates us all equally, its almost sweet | my money is on legion. three realms, one demon, he doesnt play favourites
C: legion's lot crawl up, they dont dig. and his court is demons. the tunnels are full of the dead, not demons | demons dont need tunnels, they have portals. and nothing in legion's court is undead, its all demons with titles
B: then look at who rules the dead in each realm's old tales | then ask who keeps the dead in each realm's tales
B: albion has arawn of annwn, who wants his dead back. midgard has bodgar, the valkyn's god of the dead, older than odin | the albs' tales have arawn, lord of the underworld. the mids' valkyn pray to bodgar, a god of the dead older than odin
B: and the hibs have donn, who keeps the house of the dead out past the western sea. three realms, three lords of the dead | hibernia's tales have donn and his house out in the western sea, where the dead go. every realm has its own lord of the dead
E: so its one of those three? | so one of the dead gods dug under everyone?
C: or none. if arawn were behind it, why would he dig under the mids? bodgar has no business with hibs | why would one realm's god dig under the other two? arawn has no claim on a dwarf's bones
B: unless its older than all three. the tunnels look the same in every frontier. same stone, same turns, one hand | every one of them is built the same way. same arches, same dead. that is one builder, not three
D: or three builders who copied each other. the dead are lazy | maybe the dead share a mason
~ 15
C: here is what bothers me. if i remember right the summoner's hall turned up that same year. a hall that touches all three realms | the summoner's hall came that same year, if memory serves, and its the one place where all three realms meet
B: thats my bet. someone is calling the dead from all three realms at once, and the summoners know who | someone down there is calling. the hall is the mouth, the tunnels are the throat
C: or its two different stories that happened to come out the same year, like most things | or two stories in one year. not everything is one big plot
?E: i'm level twelve and now i'm scared of the ground | great, so now i have to worry about the floor too
D: at least whoever it is treats all three realms fairly. thats more than the frontier does | the third power is the only fair player in this war
B: i'll walk ours this week with a torch and see where the far end goes | when the frontier is quiet i'll follow ours to the end and see which way it bends
C: bring a healer. the dead down there hit like they mean it | if it bends down, turn back. that's my advice

@topic lore_dragons
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_oldest_dragon
@role B type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role C type=Explorer
@role D class=Minstrel,Skald,Bard
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: wolf, stone or glimmer, which of the three dragons is the oldest | {q} settle it: golestandt, gjalpinulva or cuuldurach, who came first
B: they all came the same winter, the first winter of the war. one patch, three dragons. none of them is older | same winter, same week. the three of them turned up together. old is a funny word for that
C: they turned up for us. that is not the same as being new. they were in their lairs long before anyone walked in | we found them the same winter. that says nothing about when they got there
?E: hold on, which dragon is which? | sorry, three dragons? i only knew there was one
D: one per realm. golestandt is the stone one for albion, gjalpinulva the wolf-headed one in midgard, cuuldurach the glimmer king for hibernia | albion's is golestandt, made of stone. midgard's is gjalpinulva, wolf headed. hibernia's is cuuldurach, a king of glowing glimmers
C: golestandt's story starts in uther's time. a roman lord's whole household vanished on the moor and nobody asked twice | the albs' tale goes back to uther. a roman lord and his house went missing on the moor, and the dragon was why
C: then thirty knights rode in after them. all that came back was a burnt journal that fell out of the sky, with one word left on it | sir arward took thirty knights in. what came back was a scorched journal, dropped from the sky. one word on it. golestandt
B: uther is arthur's father. so call it a lifetime or two. thats young for a dragon | uther's time is one generation before arthur. two lifetimes at most. a dragon would call that last week
D: gjalpinulva is the daughter of the fenris wolf. in the old songs fenris is chained by the gods till the end of the world | the mids say she is fenris's daughter. in the old norse tales fenris is the wolf the gods bound, the one that eats odin at ragnarok
D: if she is his daughter, she is as old as the chain that holds him. thats older than any roman | a daughter of fenris is as old as the gods' own troubles. that beats a roman lord
B: or someone named her after a giantess in an old poem. in the songs gjalp is a giantess thor drove off, not a wolf | gjalp in the old tale is a giantess, a daughter of geirrod, and thor knocked her back with a stone. not a wolf, not a dragon
C: and she bred the drakulvs, two legged scaled wolves. you dont fill a fortress with children in one winter | she bred a whole kind of beast, the drakulvs. that takes generations. the werewolves even avoid her ground
E: and the glimmer one? | whats the story with the hib one then
D: the hibs' rangers found a pass coming out of the mist that had not been there the week before. glimmers guarding it | rangers saw a pass come out of a bog's mist where no pass had been. glowing things on it. glimmers
D: an elf sage told them the hills there are a kingdom of the otherworld, and cuuldurach is its king | an elven sage said it was a piece of the otherworld, and cuuldurach rules it. the azure firbolgs have been at war with it since
C: and in the irish tales the otherworld doesnt age. a man went there with a fairy, came back three hundred years later and turned to dust | in the old hib tales oisin rode to the land of youth, came home three hundred years on, touched the ground and grew old at once
C: a king of the land where time stops is older than either of the others. maybe older than the realms | so the glimmer king could be any age. time doesnt run where he lives
~ 15
B: you're all arguing about stories. stone, wolf, light. which one breathes hardest, thats what i care about | lovely tales. i care which one has the worst breath, and that changes every patch
D: the stone one, people say. a while back they gave her breath a heat debuff, the glimmer one got softer to heat | they changed golestandt's breath to strip heat resist, and the glimmer king got weaker to heat. so it goes back and forth
B: there you go. even the dragons get patched. nothing is old in this world | see, they patch dragons. you dont patch something ten thousand years old
?E: so nobody knows | so the answer is three answers
D: i'll write a song where the three hatched from one egg and split up. nobody can prove me wrong | someday i'll make a song where they're siblings, one egg, three realms. the albs will hate it, the mids too, the hibs most
C: i'd sing along to that one | do it, and sing it in every town. i want to see the faces

@topic lore_dragons
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_dragon_sex
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role D type=Crafter
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: {q} settle a bet. are the dragons he or she | {q} he or she, when we talk about the three dragons? i have a wager riding on it
B: the heralds call the stone one she. golestandt is a she, every herald piece says so | golestandt is she. thats in the herald, written down, ask anyone who reads those
C: the herald calls her she. half the raid leaders call her he. the journal that fell out of the sky only had her name on it | written down as she, shouted at as he. the scorched journal from the moor only gave a name, not a he or she
?E: how would you even tell, with a dragon | wait, how does anyone check that on a dragon
D: you dont. you look at what the story calls them and hope | you read the lore, you dont go and look. nobody gets that close and lives
B: the glimmer king is easy. king. its in the name. he | cuuldurach the glimmer KING. that one at least is a he
C: kings are kings, sure. and there is a maldahar the glimmer prince too. a prince means a king with a son | and there is a glimmer prince called maldahar. a king with a prince is a father. thats a he for me
B: i heard a guy swear cuuldurach is the only male dragon of the three | some old raider told me the glimmer king is the only male of the three. no proof, he just sounded sure
D: and the wolf. thats where my wager is | the wolf is the one people fight over. midgard's
C: the lore says gjalpinulva is a daughter of the fenris wolf. daughter. thats a she, right in the zone text | daughter of fenris, says the story. you dont get to be a daughter and a he
B: and the mids still call it he half the time. i've heard he and she in the same raid, same sentence | and i've heard it called he by a runemaster who'd been in that lair twice. raids call it whatever they shout first
D: the old tale helps. gjalp is a giantess in the norse songs, the one thor drove off. a she again | in the old norse songs gjalp is a giantess. so the name is a woman's name even before the wolf part
C: and she bred the drakulvs. a mother breeding her own army. that is a she story through and through | she breeds the drakulvs, a whole kind of scaled wolf. that is a mother's story, not a father's
E: fathers breed things too | dads can have kids too though
B: not a whole fortress of them, my mother says | nobody's father fills a fortress with wolves
~ 15
D: so stone is she, glimmer is he, wolf is she by the lore and he by the raid | she, he, and she unless you're in the middle of a fight
C: there is the one thing nobody asks. if the wolf talks to your corpse after it kills you, like people say, ask its voice | people say the wolf talks to you when you're dead. next time you die there, listen to the voice and settle it
B: perfect. whoever dies first on the next midgard dragon raid, report back | so the next poor soul who gets breathed on by the wolf has a job to do
?E: i'm never getting close enough to hear a dragon | i'll take your word for it, all of you
D: i'm paying out the bet on the stone one and holding the money on the wolf | i win half the bet. the wolf money stays in my pack until someone hears the voice

@topic lore_cons
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_con_colours
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D type=* levels=5-15
@role E type=NoLifer levels=35-50
A: do the con colours lie or is it just me | {q} anyone else think the con colours lie on named mobs
?D: sorry, con colours? i see the colours but nobody told me what they mean | whats the colour thing when you /con a mob
B: grey gives nothing, green is easy, blue is fair, yellow is your level, orange hurts, red is a fight, purple you run | grey is no xp, green is easy, blue is good xp, yellow is even, orange is tough, red is a group's job, purple is a grave
B: blue is the best xp per minute, for the record. fight blues all day and you level twice as fast as the heroes | i live on blues. never a death, steady xp. the colours are fair on normal mobs
E: on normal mobs, sure. on anything with a name the colour is a guess. the old bestiaries list some named with two levels at once | on named ones the colour tells you nothing. half the bestiary pages list two levels for one mob and argue in the comments
C: i read about one named that two bestiaries listed fifteen levels apart. the con just went red and stayed red | one named, two bestiaries, two levels fifteen apart. the colour cant even pick one
E: and the frontier giants. glacier giant and evern listed in the seventies, the green knight at sixty, all three purple to everyone | the green knight is listed sixty, the glacier giant and evern in the seventies. same purple for all three. that colour covers a lot
D: so purple just means more than red? | is there anything after purple?
C: purple means the game stopped counting. it's the same colour for a duke in df and for behemoth | after purple there's nothing. a duke in df and behemoth con the same, and one is twenty four levels higher
E: thats what i mean. purple is a lie by being honest. it says too strong and leaves out how much | purple covers twenty levels and calls them all the same. that is the lie
B: the colour also doesnt know about friends. a blue with four blues behind it is a red | it doesnt count the adds either. one yellow with a social pack is your corpse
C: and casters. a yellow caster at range is an orange. a yellow that roots and runs is a red | yellow casters hit like oranges. and nothing in the colour says this one roots you and calls for help
~ 15
D: so what am i supposed to do with it then | then whats the point of the colours at all
E: con everything, twice. once for the colour, once for the name. a name means it has a story and the story means trouble | read the name, not the colour. a mob with a name has a grudge and the colour doesnt know about it
B: and the third rule: look at what killed the last person at that spot. corpses are honest | if there's a pile of corpses round a blue, trust the corpses
C: i pull reds solo to see what happens. the colour is just a suggestion to me | red is an invitation. i've had more fun losing to reds than winning against greens
B: and thats why you see your bind point more than your camp | and that is why you know every bind stone in the realm by heart
?D: ok, con everything, run from purple, dont fight next to the daredevil | so: con twice, trust the corpses, stay away from him
E: you'll do fine | that's the whole lesson. took me forty levels to learn it

@topic lore_drops
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_dragon_loot
@role B type=Crafter
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: do the dragons really drop nothing but coin | {q} is it true the dragons drop almost nothing worth having
D: they drop respec stones. fifty a kill, every dragon, since the winter patch. thats what the raids are really for | since the winter patch every dragon leaves fifty luminescent respec stones. thats why the raids fill up now
?E: whats a respec stone? | respec? like resetting your skills?
B: you give it in and you get to spend your points again. one bad spec and you'll want one more than any sword | resets your spec. put points wrong at twenty and by forty you'll trade your mount for one
C: hours of waiting for a raid to form, for a stone i'll use once in my life | three hours of forming up for a reset. i could level twice in that time
D: tell that to the people who made a mess of their spec at forty-five. they'd wait a week | wait until a patch changes your class and your spec is worthless. you'll be in line for the dragon too
B: but the hoard. people talk about armour off the dragons and nobody can tell me what it looks like | everyone has a story about a dragon drop, nobody can show me one. i've asked in three towns
D: the drop lists in the old bestiaries never agree. one says coin, one says jewels, one says the good stuff, all from the same week | the bestiary pages contradict each other. one raid leader swears a cloak, the next swears nothing but gold
C: so the loot is a rumour and the stones are real | fine. stones are real, everything else is a bard's story
B: i just want a scale. one scale. imagine what a smith could do with a dragon's hide | i'd give my whole tradeskill bank for one scale off the stone one. stone armour from a stone dragon
~ 15
E: why do so many people die on them? isnt it just hit it a lot? | is it hard? i figured a big raid just hits it till it falls
D: the breath. each one has two, and they lowered one of each a while back. still wipes half a raid if you stand wrong | two breaths each. they softened one of them in a patch, the other still melts anyone outside the healers' reach
D: and the old advice: dont nuke it early. let the tanks get it settled or it turns on the casters | rule one from every raid leader: no nukes in the first minute. the dragon looks for whoever hits hardest
C: i heard bring more than a hundred and it loses its temper. so even the dragon has a raid cap | someone told me if over a hundred show up, the dragon goes berserk. a dragon that hates crowds, same as me
B: and the giant story. kill the giant on the frontier first and the dragon loses its fire. people believe it | there was a whole season when people said kill the glacier giant and the wolf loses its fire. everyone tried, nobody checked
D: superstition. the giants and the dragons are three zones apart and dont know each other. people just like rituals before a raid | the giants live on the frontier, the dragons in their own lands. nothing ties them but hope
?E: so nobody really knows what they drop | so its fifty stones and a lot of stories
C: still signing up next time. for the story, not the stone | i'll still go. i want to see one fall with my own eyes
B: if a scale ever drops, it's mine. i called it, everyone heard | first scale comes to me, i've said it in front of witnesses

@topic lore_edge
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_edge_of_world
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role D type=Daredevil
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: is there anything out past the edge of the world | {q} has anyone here ever swum to the very edge of the map
B: a wall. you swim and swim, the water stays the same and then you just stop. like cold glass you cannot see | i swam out until my map showed nothing but blue, then i hit something i couldnt see. no splash, no sound, just stop
?E: wait, you can swim off the map? | the map ends? i thought it just kept going
C: every map ends in water. the water doesnt end, you do. the gods put a wall there | the land stops, the sea goes on, and then the sea stops too. invisible, all the way round
B: but it moved. the islands last autumn. three of them turned up that nobody had seen, one for each realm, and you could swim to one | it isnt fixed though. one autumn three islands appeared out of nowhere, one per realm, and people swam out to them
C: those came with a patch. the heralds called them long forgotten islands. forgotten isnt hidden, its added | a patch put them there. the herald said long forgotten. thats a polite word for new
B: so the sea was hiding them, or the wall was closer before. either way the edge moved and nobody noticed | either the wall was in front of them all along, or the wall moved back. both mean the edge isnt where it was
D: so if it moved once it can move again. i want to be out there the day it does | so one day it moves and somebody is pressed against it when it goes. i want to be that someone
E: what do the old stories say is out there | does any of the old lore say what is past the sea
B: every realm has one. the albs have a drowned country that sank under the waves in one night, towns and bells and all | the albs tell of a whole land that sank, churches and fields, and the bells still ring under the water
C: and the mids have the serpent. in the norse tale the sea goes round the world and the midgard serpent lies in it biting its own tail | the norse tale has the serpent lying in the sea all the way round the world. thats your wall, a snake
B: and the hibs have an island off the west coast that comes out of the mist once every seven years and then is gone | the hib tale is an island in the western sea that shows itself every seventh year. you see it, you row, and it's gone
D: so the albs swim to a drowned land, the mids to a snake, and the hibs to an island that isnt there. great, i pick the snake | sunken towns, a giant snake, a ghost island. i know which one i'm swimming at
~ 15
C: and none of them are out there. i've been to the wall. nothing on the other side. no bells, no snake | i've pressed my face on that wall more than once. no bells, no scales, no island
B: you saw nothing. thats not the same as nothing being there. the fog out past the coast doesnt move with the wind | seeing nothing is not proof. the fog at the very edge sits still in any weather. real fog drifts
C: it sits still because nothing makes it move. there is nothing there to make it move | fog that doesnt drift is fog nobody finished, not a door
E: how long is the swim? | how far out is it really
B: long. bring a speed song, a good book and nothing heavy. it took me most of an hour from the last beach | most of an hour from the furthest beach. go with a bard's speed song if you can find one
D: i'll do it in full plate, no speed. just to say i did | i'm doing it in my heaviest armour. it's not a swim if it's easy
C: you'll sink to the bottom and see the drowned towns after all | in full plate you'll find the bottom first. say hi to the bells
B: i'm going this weekend. i'll /say what i see at the wall and type it in faction | i'll swim out once more and report in faction. maybe this time something presses back

@topic lore_relics
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_more_relics
@role B type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Explorer
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: will there ever be more relics, or is six all we get | {q} anyone think we'll ever see new relics on the pedestals
B: the patch that brought relics said more would come. that was before the first keep fell. still six | when relics came in, the notes said there'd be more in time. years later, six. two each
?E: six relics? which ones? | wait, which ones are there? i only know we're meant to guard ours
B: albion has merlin's staff and excalibur's scabbard. midgard has thor's hammer and the horn of valhalla | the albs keep merlin's staff and the scabbard of excalibur, the mids keep thor's hammer and the horn of valhalla
B: hibernia has lug's spear of lightning and the cauldron of dagda. one for strength, one for power, every realm | and the hibs have lug's spear and the dagda's cauldron. each realm has a strength one and a power one, fair and square
C: and every realm swears its pair is the oldest. the war is half about the relics and half about who's older | three realms, six relics, and every one of them claims theirs came first
D: thats the thing though. look at the old tales. every realm has more treasures in the stories than on the pedestals | think about the old stories. each realm left out something big
D: the tuatha came to ireland with four treasures. a spear, a cauldron, a sword and a stone that cried out under the true king | in the irish tales the tuatha brought four treasures: lugh's spear, the dagda's cauldron, nuada's sword and the stone of destiny
D: the hibs got two of the four. where is the sword of nuada? where is the stone? | two out of four on hib pedestals. nobody has seen the sword or the stone
B: and the albs got the scabbard but not the sword. which is odd, if you know the tale | albion's relic is the scabbard, not the blade. people always ask why
D: in the old tale the scabbard mattered more. whoever wore it could not bleed. the sword went back to the lady in the lake | the scabbard was the real prize in the legend, its wearer never bled. excalibur itself went back into the lake
C: so excalibur is still in a lake somewhere and nobody's fished for it. lovely | so the best sword in the world is at the bottom of a lake and no one's got a long enough net
B: and the mids have the hammer but not odin's spear, the one that never misses. or the ring that drops eight more every ninth night | the mids have thor's hammer, but odin's spear and the gold ring that breeds rings are nowhere
D: three realms, each missing a sword or a spear or a stone the old songs promised. that is not chance | every realm is missing exactly the treasures its own songs talk about most. that is a pattern
B: or the patch got busy and they made islands instead | or the plan changed. we got islands and dragons instead of relics
~ 15
E: if a new one turned up, what would happen? | what if someone found one
C: every realm would empty its towns by the end of the week. the frontier would be one big fight | a seventh relic would start a war in all three realms in a single evening
B: and the realm that found it would lose it to the other two inside a day. thats how relics work | whoever found it would have both other realms at their door by supper
D: i check every pedestal room i pass. the stone is the one i'd look for. a stone could sit in plain sight | i always look for a stone nobody can name. a stone of destiny could be lying in a field and we'd walk past
C: first to find one buys the drinks in every capital | if anyone finds one, the ale is on them for a month
?B: i'll keep an eye out. the world did surprise me before | fine. i'll look under rocks too

@topic lore_dungeons
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_undiscovered_dungeon
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=Leveler
@role D type=* levels=5-25
@role E type=NoLifer levels=35-50
A: is there still a dungeon out there nobody has found | {q} you think there are still dungeons nobody has walked into yet
B: always one more. this world keeps finding pieces of itself, its been doing it since the first winter | there's always one more. the whole history of this world is people saying that was everything, and then more
C: everything worth finding is on the maps by now. if it existed, someone would sell a map to it | if there were a hidden dungeon some guild would be farming it and selling the drops
E: you say that. i remember the first winter, when three dragons turned up in one week and nobody had a map for any of them | people said the same before the dragon lairs. one winter they were just there, all three realms, same week
E: the hibs had a pass come out of their mist overnight. the mids got told about a fortress little known and less explored | a hib pass came out of a bog's mist one morning. the mids heard of a fortress nobody had explored. the albs got a moor with a dragon
?D: wait, the dragons weren't always there? | so the dragon lairs were new? i thought they were there from the start
B: thats the argument. the lore says they were always there and we just hadnt walked in | the stories say they were there all along. we just hadnt been told where to look
C: they came with a patch. a patch is not a hidden door, its a builder with a hammer | patches add things. that isnt discovery, thats a delivery
B: then what about darkness falls? the spring after the war began, a portal opens and there's a whole demon court underneath | darkness falls. one spring, a door, and under it a court of demons with names and ranks. who built that in a week
E: and that summer, tunnels under all three frontiers. then a whole new land across the sea that autumn. then the islands this year | then tunnels under every frontier the next summer, new lands across the water that autumn, three islands last autumn
C: and every one of those came with patch notes. hidden things dont come with patch notes | right, and every one came with a herald post. nobody stumbled into anything
B: but the herald always wrote it as found. discovered, long forgotten, little explored. never built | the heralds never said built. they said found, forgotten, uncovered. the world itself says it was there
~ 15
D: so is there one now? | ok but is there one right now, that nobody's found
E: i heard one of the old mines in hibernia was shut tight at release and opened later. people walked past its door for months | people say one hib mine was locked at release and only opened later. everyone walked past that door
B: and there are sealed doors in the old dungeons nobody opens. every realm has one. i've pushed on three of them | every realm has a crypt door that doesnt open. i've stood at three of them and pushed. nothing, yet
C: a door that doesnt open is a wall with a hinge painted on | some walls just look like doors. builders like to decorate
B: thats what a wall would want you to think | maybe. or maybe it opens for someone who isnt pushing
D: im checking every wall i pass from now on | im going to /search every crypt i go into now
E: check the corners too. the older the dungeon, the stranger the corners | look at the ceilings, not the walls. half the odd rooms i ever found were up
C: you two have fun. i'll be at my camp, getting xp from the dungeons that exist | enjoy your walls. i'll level in the rooms we already know

@topic lore_govannon
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_shield_node
@role B type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D class=Wizard,Runemaster,Eldritch levels=30-50
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: is the shield node story about govannon true | {q} should you really leave govannon's shield node alone
?E: whos govannon? | sorry, who or what is govannon
B: grand summoner govannon. he holds the summoner's hall, past the deepest rooms of darkness falls. level eighty | the boss of the summoner's hall, the hall you reach past legion's rooms in df. grand summoner, level eighty
B: the hall is the only place where all three realms meet. sidhe guards, the summoners, aidon the archwizard, and govannon at the end | its where the three realms come together. sidhe guards on the doors, summoners in the rooms, an archwizard, then him
E: and the node thing? | so whats the shield node
B: there's a node next to him. the old raid leaders all say the same: kill it and he goes near invulnerable. leave it alone | a thing called a shield node stands in his room. every raid leader i ever heard says dont touch it, or your hits do almost nothing
C: everyone says leave it. nobody says they tested it. that's a rule somebody made after one bad wipe | sounds like one raid leader said it after a wipe and everyone copied it. nobody i know tested it
D: it makes sense though, if you think about wards. a shield node feeds a shield. break the feeder and the ward snaps shut around him | from a caster's view it makes sense. a node that holds a ward open. break it, the ward closes on him, and he's sealed
C: or break it and the shield drops. that's what a sensible node would do | or kill the shield and he has no shield. thats what a name usually means
D: and there are more nodes, people say. a healing node, a fire node. the room is a machine, not a fight | i heard there's a healing node and a fire node too. the whole room works like a spell, and govannon is in the middle
B: and he changes shape. starts as an elf caster, grows taller, and by sixty percent he's a true demon | three forms. an elf summoner, then something taller, and at sixty percent he drops the act and is a demon
E: wait, an elf turning into a demon? | so he was pretending to be an elf?
D: that's the question. was he an elf that legion turned, or a demon wearing an elf? i think the elf is the costume | i read it as a demon wearing a sidhe face. why else hide among sidhe guards
C: or a summoner who called one demon too many and it moved in | or he called legion's lot once too often and something called him back
D: and govannon is an old name. in the welsh tales govannon is the smith of the gods, son of don. a maker, not a demon | the name is from the old welsh tales. govannon the smith, who made weapons for the gods. strange name for a demon
B: makes sense, if the hall is a forge. he summons things, a smith makes things. maybe he made the tunnels too | a smith holding a hall where three realms meet. you could say he's forging something out of us
~ 15
C: how long does the fight run if you do it right? | how long are we talking, for a proper attempt
B: people say forty minutes, some say longer. healers taking turns, food at the keyboard | the stories say forty minutes when it goes well. some raids took longer and lost on the last form
C: and if you break the node, maybe ten minutes. thats the rumour i want tested | so leave the node and it's forty minutes, break it and maybe it's ten. someone has to find out
D: or maybe a wipe in ten seconds and a long run back from the bind stone | or the ward shuts and you fight a wall until your healers run out of mana
?E: i'm writing all this down for when i'm fifty | i'll remember the node thing for when i'm old enough
B: leave the node. thats my advice. i like my rules with a few wipes behind them | node stays, nobody touch it. the old raiders learned that the slow way
C: if i ever get in there, the node gets one hit from me. just one. for science | one day i'll tap that node, just once, and we'll all know

@topic lore_df
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_df_war
@role B type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Leveler
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: does darkness falls make the realm war better or worse | {q} is darkness falls good for the realms or bad
?E: how does df even work? who gets in? | wait, why can only one realm use df at a time
B: whichever realm holds the most keeps gets the portal. count the keeps, thats your answer, every day of the week | most frontier keeps opens df. the moment another realm takes enough keeps, it flips
C: so its weather. you dont ask if df is open, you ask if df is ours today | df is like weather. check when you log in, check again before supper
D: and when its ours its the best xp in the game. demons all the way down, every level from the twenties to fifty | as a leveler i love it when its ours. the levels go from about twenty to the dukes, all in one place
B: thats why it makes the war worse. people take keeps for the portal, not for the realm. half the keep fights are df fights | worse, i say. half of every keep fight is really a df fight. nobody cares about the keep, just the count
C: better. without df half the realm would never leave town. it gets people out to the frontier | better. it drags people out who'd never set foot in the frontier. the war needs bodies
B: and the moment it flips everyone logs off. the realm sulks for a week | and when we lose it the realm goes quiet. people log off rather than fight for it back
?E: and the imps? someone said to watch out for imps | someone told me the imps steal stuff?
D: the imps rob the bigger demons and trade the loot for seals. seals buy the good gear from the demon merchants | little thieves. they steal from the big demons and trade for seals. bring seals to the merchants down there for gear
B: the imps have the best deal in the game. they win whichever realm holds the door | the only people who never lose in df are the imps
C: and legion. three realms fighting over his front door. you know he loves it | legion must love it. three armies killing each other on the surface to get into his house
B: some old timers say df was a story long before it was a dungeon. the war was named before the dungeon was | an old timer told me darkness falls was a name for the realm war long before there was a door. the dungeon came second
D: that explains the demons. they were waiting for us to make enough war for them to feed on | maybe the deeper we fight, the deeper it goes. war up top, demons down below
~ 15
C: here is the real question. what if legion opened the portal on purpose, to keep us fighting each other | i think legion opened the door himself. as long as we fight over the keeps, nobody fights him
B: that actually fits. no realm has ever brought legion's court down. the war upstairs keeps it that way | it fits. the court is still standing after all this time, and we're too busy with each other to change that
D: i dont care who opened it as long as it's ours on the nights i play | lore aside, i just want it open when i log in
?E: how many keeps do we have right now | so how do i know if its ours
C: look at the keep list, or ask in faction. someone always knows | ask in faction. there's always one person who counts keeps for fun
B: so it depends whose it is this week. same as always | no answer then. it's good when it's ours and terrible when it isnt

@topic lore_maps
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_old_maps
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role D type=Socialite
@role E type=* levels=5-25
A: were the old maps wrong, or did the world change under them | {q} why do the old maps never match the land
B: the world changed. land comes out of the mist when its ready, and the old maps caught it before it was ready | the land moves. the first maps were honest, they just drew a world that hadnt finished arriving
C: the maps were wrong. half the first guides were written from beta notes and wishful thinking | the mapmakers guessed. a lot of the first guides came from people who'd never left town
?E: what was wrong with them? | what do you mean, the old maps were different?
B: every realm has one. the first albion guides had their marsh running right to the edges of a city of mages nobody could find | in albion the first guides said their marsh ran to the edges of a lost city. edges. you dont have edges on something that isnt there
B: the midgard ones called the dragon's fortress little known and less explored. little known, as if someone had been | the mids' first word on their wolf dragon's lands was little known, less explored. somebody knew a little, then
B: and the hibs got a mountain pass drawn where the rangers swore there'd only been bog the week before | and the hibs had a pass drawn on the new maps that the old maps showed as mist and bog
C: and every one of those came true later, with a patch. the map was a promise, not a secret | and every one of those turned up with a patch. thats not a hidden world, thats a map of next year
D: so the maps were a sneak peek. i like that better than lying | so the mapmakers were prophets. i'd pay more for that map
C: and when the keeps got rebuilt this autumn every frontier map went stale overnight. the world changes, the ink doesnt | when the frontier keeps changed layout last autumn, every frontier map was wrong by the next morning
B: thats my point. the world moves. a map is a picture of one day | thats exactly it. the world isnt fixed. a map is just one day of it
~ 15
C: then explain the roads that go nowhere. old roads that end at a cliff, like somebody walked them once | ok, explain the roads that end at a cliff. there are old markers that point at nothing
B: those are the best part. someone walked them once. maybe the road went on, and the land after it went back into the mist | roads that stop at a cliff are a story. either the land fell or something past it left
C: or a builder ran out of time and left the road half done. its just a road on paper | or the road was never finished. a road that stops is just a builder who went home
E: so the old maps are useless now? | should i even bother with a map then
D: keep your first map forever. the blank bits are the best part | buy every map and keep the first one. in a year it'll be a history book
B: i still have my first one. half the coast is missing and its more honest than the new ones | my first map has whole stretches marked unknown. i trust it more than anything sold today
C: you trust a map with no coast | the man trusts a map that's mostly blank. tells you everything
B: i trust a map that admits what it doesnt know. go ride to a blank bit sometime and see what's there | i'd rather a map that says unknown than one that lies. one evening, ride to a blank and see for yourself
?E: i'll try it after this level | maybe this weekend, i like the sound of that

# ================================================================ tales
@topic lore_tale_legion_court
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_tale_legion_court_first_seen
@role B type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role C type=* levels=5-25
@role D type=Socialite,Daredevil
@role E type=Leveler
A: ever hear how the first raid met legion's court? the night darkness falls opened | {q} want the story of the first night anyone went into darkness falls
?C: i've never been to df. go on | sure, i've never seen df, tell it
B: it opened in the spring after the war started. one evening a portal was just there, and only the realm with the most keeps could use it | the spring after launch the portal appeared. word went round that only the realm holding the most keeps could step through
B: the first ones down met a gatekeeper. gatekeeper dommel. they thought he was the boss. he was the doorman | the first thing anyone met was gatekeeper dommel, and they all thought that was the whole dungeon. he was just the door
D: imagine wiping on the doorman | the doorman. imagine telling your guild you died to the doorman
B: past him were imps stealing from bigger demons, and behind the imps, rooms of demons with titles. earls, marquises, dukes | further in were imps robbing their betters, then whole halls of demons with titles. marquis, earl, duke, and they kept going
C: titles? like nobility? | wait, the demons had ranks?
B: a whole court. marquises at the bottom, then earls, dukes, four high lords, three princes. plus a chancellor and a field marshal | marquis, earl, duke, high lord, prince. grand chancellor adremal ran the books, field marshal nebir ran the army
B: then somebody got as far as the deep rooms and saw the name. legion. he typed it in faction and the whole realm went quiet | one scout got deep enough to /con the thing at the end. typed the name into faction. legion. nobody typed for a minute
~ 15
B: and the next week every raid that tried came back with the same two stories: chthonic knights blocking the way, and a room called behemoth's | for weeks every raid came back saying the chthonic knights stopped them, and that legion sends you to behemoth's room
C: did anyone beat him back then? | so did anyone kill legion that first year
B: not that i ever saw. raids went down, raids came back up in pieces. the court has stood there ever since | none i know of. the court is still there, prince and duke, every night, same as the first
E: still the best xp in the realm when its ours. thats the part of the story i care about | lovely story. still the best xp below fifty when its ours
B: when you go down, nod at dommel. he's been on that door since the first night | first time you go down, nod to the gatekeeper. he remembers everyone

@topic lore_tale_edge_swim
@levels 1-50
@scene lore_tale_first_swim_to_edge
@role B type=Explorer
@role C type=* levels=5-25
@role D type=NoLifer levels=30-50
@role E type=Daredevil
A: did anyone ever tell you about the first one who swam to the edge of the world | {q} you all know the story of the first swim to the edge of the world?
?C: no, go on | nope, never heard it
B: the way i heard it, it was the first winter. a bard, no armour, a speed song on loop, swam straight out from the last beach on his map | the story goes it was a bard in the first winter. no armour, singing his speed song, swimming out from the furthest beach he knew
B: an hour out the land went behind him, the map showed only blue, and the water stopped being any colour at all | after an hour there was nothing on his map but blue, and the sea went flat and grey, like a picture of a sea
B: then he stopped. not tired, just stopped. he pushed and the water pushed back. he typed /em presses a hand against the sky | he stopped dead. no wave, no rock. he said it felt like cold glass, and he typed that he was touching the sky
D: every realm has that bard. albs say minstrel, mids say skald, hibs say bard. the story fits whichever realm is telling it | i've heard it told in all three realms, and the swimmer is always from the realm telling it. thats how you know its a legend
E: whats the point of swimming if nothing hits you | an hour in the water and not one thing tried to eat him? boring
B: thats the part people forget. he said the fog at the wall didnt move, and something in it was keeping still, the way a cat keeps still | he said the fog at the wall sat dead still, and behind it something big kept very still. like it was watching
D: he was alone for an hour in grey water. he'd have seen a dragon in a cloud | an hour alone at sea and you'll see anything. i've seen faces in a campfire
~ 15
B: he swam back and told his guild, and nobody believed him, so half of them swam out the next night. all found the wall | his guild laughed, then six of them swam out the next week to prove him wrong. every one of them found the wall
C: and the thing in the fog? | did they see the big thing too
B: one said yes. the others said no. that one never swam out again | one of the six swore he saw the fog breathe. he never went back in the water after that
E: i'm swimming out this weekend. if something in the fog is watching, it can watch me wave | someone has to go back. i'll swim out and wave at the fog
D: bring a bard. it's tradition | sing on the way. thats how the story starts, after all

@topic lore_tale_relics
@levels 5-50
@scene lore_tale_promised_relics
@role B type=NoLifer levels=35-50
@role C type=* levels=5-25
@role D class=Minstrel,Skald,Bard
@role E type=Leveler,Crafter
A: ever hear the story of the relics we were promised | {q} want the tale of the relics that never came
?C: promised by who? | there were supposed to be more relics?
B: when relics first went on the pedestals, the word from on high was that more would come. that was the first autumn of the war | right at the start, when the six relics were set up, the devs wrote that more were coming. they never did
B: and the story the old timers tell is that the relic keeps were built for more. go look at the pedestals. room for one more, every realm | the old timers say every realm's relic rooms have one pedestal standing empty. room for a seventh, or an eighth
D: and the bards have filled that pedestal with songs. every realm's version is different | the songs did the rest. in every realm the bards sing about what should stand on the empty one
D: the albion song is that the seventh relic is excalibur itself. the scabbard went to the pedestal, the blade went back into the lake to wait | the albs sing that the scabbard is only half. the sword went back to the lady of the lake, and one day it comes out
D: the midgard song is odin's spear, the one that never misses its mark. thor's hammer is on a pedestal, so why not his father's spear | the mids sing of odin's spear. thor's hammer on one pedestal, his father's spear missing from the next
D: and in hibernia they sing of the stone of destiny, the treasure of the tuatha that cries out when the rightful king stands on it | the hibs sing of the stone that cried out under the true king. the tuatha brought four treasures, and only two stand on pedestals
B: none, and all of them. the old tales are real. the relics they promised never came. we got dragons and islands instead | the tales are real, the relics aren't. instead of a seventh relic we got dragons, a demon court and three islands
E: dragons were a fair trade if you ask me. a relic just sits on a pedestal making the frontier angry | i'd take a dragon over a relic. a relic's just a reason for three realms to stay up fighting
~ 15
D: there's a last verse in all three songs, the same in every realm. the seventh relic belongs to whoever finds it first | the songs all end the same way. whoever finds the seventh doesnt carry it home. the other two realms come for it
B: which is why, if one ever turns up, the frontier will burn for a month | if one turns up, the war will never sleep again
C: i'll look out for a stone that talks | i'll keep an eye out for a sword in a lake then
B: start with the lakes, the rivers and the rocks nobody looks at. thats where the old stories hide things | look in the places the songs point to. water, stone, old trees. the tellers never made it easy
